# 4. Your weekly study routine

Since you're working, I wouldn't recommend studying randomly. Use a consistent routine.

Assuming 12 hours per week:

| Activity                     | Hours/week |
| ---------------------------- | ---------- |
| Theory and mathematics       | 3          |
| Practical implementation     | 5          |
| Reading papers/documentation | 1          |
| Project development          | 2          |
| Revision and notes           | 1          |
| Total                        | 12         |

My preferred learning approach:

1. Understand the concept.
2. Study the mathematical intuition.
3. Implement a small example.
4. Experiment with different configurations.
5. Build something using the concept.
6. Document what you learned.

For example, when studying self-attention, don't immediately jump into Hugging Face. Implement scaled dot-product attention in PyTorch first.

That small implementation will help you understand what happens inside the Transformer.

